## 2. State-of-the-Art Research Synthesis (2024 to 2026)

1. **Proxy-First Coarse-to-Fine Conditioning (Era3D / MV-Adapter Pattern)**:
   - Generating final multi-view detail straight from a single RGB cutout is mathematically ill-posed. Modern multi-view synthesis (Era3D row-wise epipolar attention, MV-Adapter unified camera+geometry condition encoders, ControlNet Depth+Normal) conditions the image generator on **rendered orthographic clay/depth/normal proxies** rather than text descriptions of camera angles.
2. **Feed-Forward Geometric Priors via VGGT / Marigold V2 (Priors Only, Never Raw Output)**:
   - **VGGT (CVPR 2025 Best Paper)** recovers camera pose (extrinsics + intrinsics), dense depth maps, and point tracks across 1 to N views in under 1 second in a single forward pass without brittle SfM/COLMAP failure on untextured grey armor.
   - **Marigold V2 (Diffusion Transformer Normals + Depth + IID)** gives razor-sharp monocular normal and depth maps directly from a single cropped view (`ref_cut.png`), predicting the true orientation of oblique bevels, concave pockets, and curvature gradients before any view rotation is requested.
3. **Epipolar Lock Lines & Canonical Registration Cube**:
   - Placing faint orthographic alignment tick rails and a normalized color-coded gizmo cube (`+X Red`, `+Y Green`, `+Z Blue`) or rendered wireframe bounding box outside the grey matte margin gives multimodal image generators direct visual anchors for `front / back / left / top / bottom` camera orientation and vertical/horizontal scale lock.

